<title>JAPAN: Mitsubishi Trust problem loans (Banking acoount).</title>
<headline>Mitsubishi Trust problem loans (Banking acoount).</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mitsubishi Trust &amp; Banking Corp has disclosed its restructured loans (in billions of yen unless specified):</p>
<p>					end-Sep 96     end-Mar 96</p>
<p>  Restructured loans	    255.0	    692.7</p>
<p>  Bad loans			 346.4	     72.5</p>
<p>  Non-performing loans	  228.1	    247.1</p>
<p>  Loans to troubled clients   325.1	    278.9</p>
<p>  Total problem loans	    1.15 trln	1.29 trln</p>
<p>Restructured loans are those on which interest rates have been cut to help corporate restructuring. Bad loans are to bankrupt firms and non-performing are those with interest payments in arrears by six months or more. Loans to troubled clients are mainly to the bank's non-bank affiliates.</p>
</text>
